    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` derived field on owner responses, per the spec: **true when the owner is a possible duplicate, the email domain is disposable-adjacent, or the city is over its soft capacity; otherwise false.**\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `riskFlag` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and it's documented in the API spec.\n\n2. **`RiskFlags.java`** (new, in `rest/function/common`, alongside `MembershipLevels`, `OwnerSegments`, etc.) \u2014 computes the flag from owner state, OR-ing three signals:\n   - **possible duplicate** \u2192 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` (persisted by the existing `AssignPossibleDuplicate` step);\n   - **disposable-adjacent email** \u2192 the email domain contains a disposable-mail core label (the blocklist's `mailinator`/`tempmail`/`guerrillamail`) or a common disposable keyword \u2014 a *softer* check than the hard blocklist that already 400s exact matches;\n   - **city over soft capacity** \u2192 `owner.getCapacityWarning()` (the existing 40\u201349 soft-warning band, set by `AssignCapacityWarning` on both pipelines).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` binding `riskFlag` to `RiskFlags.of(owner)`, so the flag is derived at response time on both the create (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and read (`RespondWithOwner`) arms. No new pipeline steps were needed since the underlying signals are already populated on the owner before the responder maps it.\n\nThe new `Cp58Tests` (normal owner \u2192 `riskFlag` false), the `Cp38` email-blocklist test, and the full 70-test suite are green.",
